o i  actually wanted them to see  the same lifestyle that i that i was  enjoying so what would be an example of  something that you did  at that younger age that you look back  on now and say you just  can't believe you spent the money doing  that i would say  a lot of exotic cars jewelry um that i  did  i was a kind of car fetish when i was  very young i had five or six different  cars but i had the most expensive cars  when  we talking about mint leaf beverly's  maybach's  mercedes-benz so a lot of high-end  things i was into designer watches you  know rolex's  no timeless pieces that you can have  forever so i was into those type of  things  all right that was what you were into  but you also paid for things  for friends didn't you you went places  you went to vegas tell us about that  aspect of it well we went on lavish  trips i mean we would go on vacation  together we would go to  cancun we go to puerto rico we would go  you know different places and throughout  the united states  and i would travel with a big group of  guys i would travel with eight to ten  people with me and pay for their flights  hotel rooms  eating on the road so you have those  combinations of things you know we used  to have  real big deals at the end of those trips  all right now you're getting paid  because you're playing  professional basketball is there anybody  on the team  is there any business manager that says  wait a minute antoine  you know you're a great guy but the  money is not going to last forever  anybody try to sit down and have that  conversation well i had a financial  advisor a guy that was handling my money  but as any  young arrogant kid i didn't want to  listen to them i kind of took things in  my own  my own manner and made sure that i did  what i wanted to do with my money so  i was advised a little bit but i  definitely took things in my own manner  just through my own  um being my own ego all right so you  decide what  that this is the life for you you keep  spending the money  but then something happens the money  runs out  what happened what's the combination of  things i think one what we just talked  about the lifestyle  um i lost a significant portion of money  gambling  i used to go to vegas and gamble um i  lost the bulk of my money  um investing in real estate um in which  in 2007  2008 we went through the recession i'm  sure this is a worldwide thing that we  all went through  and i got caught up in that web and that  was that ultimately ended um  the bulk of my wealth so you add those  three things together um they played a  huge part in me losing all my finances  okay so you take those things those  three things but now you take this idea  that you want to share the story you  want to complete it because  you're at a personal bankruptcy and  you've got a movie  called gone in an instant tell us about  the film well i wanted to come out and  basically try to teach guys not just  necessarily athletes but just people in  general about having a lot of money  sometimes every  different people come into wealth in  different different areas so i wanted to  share my  going through bankruptcy i kind of got  an opportunity to do that and see  all the mistakes that i made so i want  to share those things but also tell my  story so people can see it as a learning  example  um creating a foundation for finance  literacy  um i have a book coming out at the  beginning of the year to talk about some  of the trials and tribulations that i  also went through and that so people  can understand what's going on in life  and make sure they do the right thing so  hopefully it can hit home for everybody  don't necessarily have to be an athlete  all right well i'm glad you mentioned  books because we'd like to get to know  you a little bit  more and i'd like to know for example  what is the the last book that you  have read what's the the most current  for you  think rich and grow the black choice i  was just reading it  i'm just kind 